{% comment %}
  Tag-gated section visibility (the show_section_tag setting).

  Storefront: when the section sits on a product page and the product lacks the tag,
  the section is hidden. Theme editor (request.design_mode): the section stays visible
  so it can be found and edited, with an indicator banner explaining the storefront state.

  Accepts:
  - tag: {String} section.settings.show_section_tag
  - hide_selector: {String} CSS selector that hides the whole section (e.g. '.section-<id>-padding')
  - product: {Object} product object

  Usage (render just inside the section's outer wrapper):
  {% render 'section-tag-gate', tag: section.settings.show_section_tag, hide_selector: hide_selector, product: product %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- if template contains 'product' and tag != blank -%}
  {%- unless product.tags contains tag -%}
    {%- if request.design_mode -%}
      <div
        class="section-tag-gate-note"
        style="padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0 0 8px; background: #fff8e1; border: 1px dashed #b28704; color: #6b5104; font-size: 12px; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; letter-spacing: 0.05em;"
      >
        HIDDEN ON STOREFRONT — this product is missing the tag &quot;{{ tag | escape }}&quot;. Shown in the editor so it stays editable.
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <style>
        {{ hide_selector }} {
          display: none;
        }
      </style>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endif -%}
